From db6b5bbec5c8a33a01196c5f91df3493f6fa1b8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zixuan Zhang <zixuan.zhang.uj@renesas.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 11:52:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] clk: renesas: r9a08g046: mark the MIPI DSI and LCDC clocks
 critical

The seamless boot logo relies on the LCDC/DSI pipeline U-Boot started
still running when the compositor issues its first commit.  Nothing holds
a reference on the module clocks in between: the DU, VSPD and DSI drivers
all end their probe runtime-suspended, so genpd's pm_clk has dropped them
again and clk_disable_unused() at late init gates the whole display path.

On RZ/G3L that does two things, both fatal to the picture: it clears the
CLK_ON bits in CPG_CLKON_MIPI_DSI/CPG_CLKON_LCDC, and - because these
clocks carry an MSTOP descriptor - it also raises the shared BUS_PERI_VIDEO1
module-stop bits.

Mark the five MIPI DSI and three LCDC module clocks CLK_IS_CRITICAL.  The
CCF then takes a reference at registration, which both keeps
clk_disable_unused() away and, since the disable path is never reached,
keeps the MSTOP bits clear.  U-Boot already enabled these clocks, so
rzg2l_mod_enable_crit_clock_init_mstop() finds them running and issues no
register write, i.e. the hand-over is glitch free.

The cost is that the display clocks can no longer be gated at runtime on
this SoC.  That is acceptable here: the LCDC is the reason the boot logo
exists, and no RZ/G3L use case gates it and expects the logo to survive.
---
 drivers/clk/renesas/r9a08g046-cpg.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/renesas/r9a08g046-cpg.c b/drivers/clk/renesas/r9a08g046-cpg.c
index 9d635ce5251f..a41659ca3588 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/renesas/r9a08g046-cpg.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/renesas/r9a08g046-cpg.c
@@ -817,6 +817,21 @@ static const unsigned int r9a08g046_crit_mod_clks[] __initconst = {
 	MOD_CLK_BASE + R9A08G046_GPIO_HCLK,
 	MOD_CLK_BASE + R9A08G046_WDT0_PCLK,
 	MOD_CLK_BASE + R9A08G046_DMAC_ACLK,
+	/*
+	 * The MIPI DSI and LCDC module clocks are the ones the seamless boot
+	 * logo needs left running.  Between the end of the driver probes and
+	 * the compositor's first commit nothing holds a reference on them, so
+	 * without this clk_disable_unused() would gate the clocks - and set
+	 * the shared VIDEO1 MSTOP bits - long before userspace exists.
+	 */
+	MOD_CLK_BASE + R9A08G046_MIPI_DSI_SYSCLK,
+	MOD_CLK_BASE + R9A08G046_MIPI_DSI_ACLK,
+	MOD_CLK_BASE + R9A08G046_MIPI_DSI_PCLK,
+	MOD_CLK_BASE + R9A08G046_MIPI_DSI_VCLK,
+	MOD_CLK_BASE + R9A08G046_MIPI_DSI_LPCLK,
+	MOD_CLK_BASE + R9A08G046_LCDC_CLK_A,
+	MOD_CLK_BASE + R9A08G046_LCDC_CLK_P,
+	MOD_CLK_BASE + R9A08G046_LCDC_CLK_D,
 };
 
 static const unsigned int r9a08g046_critical_resets[] = {
